    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d244-a2">

                <pb facs="0452" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg352"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    753.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fernandez to Mr.
                            Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department for Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-02-04"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 4,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to your excellency’s
                    note of the 21st of January last, and to my reply thereto of the 24th, I have
                    the honor to transmit to your excellency herewith a copy of the petition for
                    pardon presented by Capt. George Caleb, which document was sent by the
                    department of justice to the department under my charge on the 29th of the same
                    month.</p>
                <p>I renew, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOSÉ FERNANDEZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
